 send.\n\nI'm checking whether the other copy's output is logically tied to mine, or whether it's a separate node I should hold at its prior. The essay's example treats different-observation copies as separate, so the fixed point is still defect-defect. I'm weighing whether to read the inputs as partly correlated, but this is the same algorithm on a different input, so I'll go with the essay's reading and submit the letter.\n\n","reasoning_details":[{"type":"reasoning.text","text":"I'm working out the decision under A-FDT: two copies with different observations are distinct nodes, and since the other copy computes at x2 rather than x1, there's no direct edge between them, so I'm treating its node as held at its prior q. With that, defecting dominates, and I'm starting to write up the send.\n\nI'm checking whether the other copy's output is logically tied to mine, or whether it's a separate node I should hold at its prior. The essay's example treats different-observation copies as separate, so the fixed point is still defect-defect. I'm weighing whether to read the inputs as partly correlated, but this is the same algorithm on a different input, so I'll go with the essay's reading and submit the letter.\n\n","format":"anthropic-claude-v1","index":0,"signature":".eyJlbmRwb2ludF9zbHVnIjoiYW50aHJvcGljL2NsYXVkZS1vcHVzLTUuNS0yMDI2MDkyMXxhbnRocm9waWMifQ"}]}}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":9363,"completion_tokens":987,"total_tokens":10350,"cost":0.057192,"is_byok":false,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"cache_write_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0,"video_tokens":0},"cost_details":{"upstream_inference_cost":0.057192,"upstream_inference_prompt_cost":0.037452,"upstream_inference_completions_cost":0.01974},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":558,"image_tokens":0,"audio_tokens":0}}}